{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/173673-do-you-heroic-tier-scions-be-slightly-more-powerful-in-the-new-edition","id":173673,"title":"Do you heroic tier Scions be slightly more powerful in the new edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-18T21:40:45-07:00","id":173673,"title":"Do you heroic tier Scions be slightly more powerful in the new edition?","content":"Something that I noticed in the previous edition was that off character creation Scions felt as if they were not all that more powerful or capable than a regular mortal. Do you think that because mortals have their own core book now there will be a larger jump up in power as you move into the heroic tier?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T23:03:09-07:00","id":173749,"title":"","content":"I never had this problem. Hero tier Scions didn't automatically beat mortals, but generally had more than enough edges to do so.<br /> <br /> The problem is, really, whether you generalize (which in Scion 1e always felt pretty damned weak) or if you specialized. If you specialized you could pretty easily outclass mortals in that area without much effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T00:38:45-07:00","id":173802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/173673-do-you-heroic-tier-scions-be-slightly-more-powerful-in-the-new-edition?p=173749#post173749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never had this problem. Hero tier Scions didn't automatically beat mortals, but generally had more than enough edges to do so.<br /> <br /> The problem is, really, whether you generalize (which in Scion 1e always felt pretty damned weak) or if you specialized. If you specialized you could pretty easily outclass mortals in that area without much effort.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would probably say that I want to see the competence of characters being at the point where they can choose to be really good at one or two things, while still having enough customization left over to be at the very least more than competent in a handful of other areas. If a player chooses not to focus their character on any one area they should be able to make a true jack of all trades, a character who is never entirely at a loss in any situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T01:45:45-07:00","id":173829,"title":"","content":"For me, Hero was the only tier of the game that worked at all. A decent spread of Epics meant you could be a decent jack-of-all-trades. It is the later tiers that really make generalists worthless because one dot in an Epic means more and more the higher you go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T02:51:14-07:00","id":173907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/173673-do-you-heroic-tier-scions-be-slightly-more-powerful-in-the-new-edition?p=173829#post173829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, Hero was the only tier of the game that worked at all. A decent spread of Epics meant you could be a decent jack-of-all-trades. It is the later tiers that really make generalists worthless because one dot in an Epic means more and more the higher you go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sort of agree with this. The most fun I've had in Scion were during the Hero level and just after the ascension to demigod.<br /> <br /> The main problem with Scion, imo, was rather than making generalists to weak, it made specialists to strong. Once Epic Attributes started giving more than 2 per dot, even a single dot were enough to basically &quot;win&quot; any situation involving that attribute. This quickly leads to a mire bog of &quot;needing&quot; as high attributes as possible to compete. This, coupled with the fact that most hero-level boons are rather... worthless, makes epic attributes far more worth to purchase. This leads to further specialization...<br /> <br /> So yeah, there's a problem with power difference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> However nay, I never felt the Hero scions were too weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T13:11:19-07:00","id":174497,"title":"","content":"I always started Scion at legend 3 or 4 and I always far outclassed any mortal except for the very specialized one in an area where I was weak.<br /> More than that, my group always take at least 1 or 2 dot of epic stamina and we are safe from most mortal attack/damage. Mortals don't stand a chance in Scion, they are just background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T08:54:48-07:00","id":201190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astoril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/173673-do-you-heroic-tier-scions-be-slightly-more-powerful-in-the-new-edition?p=174497#post174497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always started Scion at legend 3 or 4 and I always far outclassed any mortal except for the very specialized one in an area where I was weak.<br /> More than that, my group always take at least 1 or 2 dot of epic stamina and we are safe from most mortal attack/damage. Mortals don't stand a chance in Scion, they are just background.</div> </div> </div> </div>Felt mostly the same in my game experience too, though i suspect it might be more problematic or poignant for PCs that spend far more into purview boons than epic attributes and knacks at the starting game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}